chapter AFP

(* The permanent audit, as a separate build target.

   Proof_Audit.thy is not mathematics. Its ML block walks every stored fact of the
   development calling Thm_Deps.all_oracles, which traverses proof terms transitively,
   then checks for hidden hypotheses, fixed free term variables and non-definitional
   axioms. That is worth doing, but it costs a large share of the build and its verdict
   cannot change unless a theory changes, so charging it to every rebuild is waste.

   The everyday command is therefore

     isabelle build ... Sigmoid_Universal_Approximation

   and the audit is run separately, before any commit that changes a proof and before
   any release:

     isabelle build ... Sigmoid_Universal_Approximation_Audit

   Proof_Audit.thy deliberately stays in the entry's own directory and is referenced
   here by relative path. Its check that every local theory file lies in the import
   closure reads that directory, so keeping the file there is what makes the check
   cover the whole development; moving it into this one would make that check
   vacuous. Isabelle does not permit two sessions to share a directory, which is why
   only this ROOT lives here. *)
session "Sigmoid_Universal_Approximation_Audit" = "Sigmoid_Universal_Approximation" +
  options [timeout = 600, document = false, quick_and_dirty = false]
  theories
    Proof_Audit
